From: GE-Proton <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] lsteamclient: maintain Wayland overlay controller focus

On compositors rejecting InputOnly XWayland focus, Steam switches its
controller context to Desktop when the overlay opens. Guide is still received
but the overlay ignores it because its app ID does not match.

Run the guarded native focus adapter after callback retrieval, using the
game's existing Steam pipe. The adapter and bridge focus query are maintained
directly in lsteamclient/steam_overlay_focus.h and overlay_bridge/, like the
other bridge implementation files. Do not create extra threads or pipes, and
do not perform Steam IPC from the Wayland event dispatcher.

--- a/lsteamclient/unixlib.cpp
+++ b/lsteamclient/unixlib.cpp
@@ -327,6 +327,8 @@ static void (*p_Steam_ReleaseThreadLocalMemory)( int );
 static bool (*p_Steam_IsKnownInterface)( const char * );
 static void (*p_Steam_NotifyMissingInterface)( int32_t, const char * );
 
+#include "steam_overlay_focus.h"
+
 template< typename Params >
 static NTSTATUS steamclient_Steam_BGetCallback( Params *params, bool wow64 )
 {
@@ -346,6 +348,7 @@ static NTSTATUS steamclient_Steam_BGetCallback( Params *params, bool wow64 )
         params->_ret = true;
     }
 
+    overlay_focus::sync( params->pipe );
     return 0;
 }
 
